  "language": "en",
  "text": "If you look at your edits and you think that nothing like what I see on Instagram, it's probably one of these three things. Number one, a lack of direction. To create a good edit, you need to know exactly what you want your scene to look like. So if you don't have an inspiration vault the size of your house or thousands of references of what you want every single thing to look like, then you're going to get lost and your edit is not going to look that good. Number two is bad design. Design is the most important skill for video editors. And having imbalanced scenes, bad contrast or uncommon patterns all signal that you're beginner editor. And lastly, number three, it's poor post -production. Post -production is what brings your animations to life. You need to look into using effects like vignettes, blurs, chromatic aberration, noise posterize time. Now, just make sure to remember these three tips the next time your edit looks boring.",
